.TH BOOT_FROM_FLASH_ALL_DTCS_AL9.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "otsdaq-mu2e 11.03.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh \- make every JTAG-attached FPGA on this node
reload its flash image, then reset PCIe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh
.RB [ NORESET ]
.RB [ NOKILL ]
.RI [ dryrun ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh
throws away a volatile bitstream loaded by
.BR program_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1)
and returns each FPGA to the image stored in its configuration flash.
That image is the one written by
.BR program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1).
.PP
The script sources
.IR /home/xilinx/Vivado_Lab/2021.2/settings64.sh .
It scans
.I /sys/bus/usb/devices
for the same USB JTAG adapters as the programming scripts
.RB ( 0403:6014 ", " 03fd:0013 ", " 03fd:0008 ).
For the
.IR N th
adapter it runs, in the current working directory:
.PP
.EX
vivado_lab \-mode batch \-source dir/boot_from_flash_one_DTC.tcl \-tclargs N
.EE
.PP
The Tcl script opens hardware target
.I N
and issues
.B boot_hw_device
on its device 0.
.PP
Unless
.B NORESET
is given, the script then runs
.B sudo
.IB dir /reset_PCIe_AL9.sh
(with
.B NOKILL
if given).
.I dir
is this script's directory, after resolving one level of symbolic link.
Unlike the programming scripts, it calls nothing in
.IR /home/mu2ehwdev .
It takes no lock and writes no line to
.IR vivado_user_log.txt .
There is no confirmation prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B NORESET
Must be the first argument.
Skips the PCIe reset.
.TP
.B NOKILL
Must be the first argument, or the second after
.BR NORESET .
It is passed to
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1).
.TP
.I dryrun
Any other non-empty first positional argument.
The
.BR source ,
Vivado and reset commands are printed, not run.
A mistyped keyword, for example
.BR noreset ,
is therefore taken as a dry run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB dir /boot_from_flash_one_DTC.tcl
Vivado Tcl, from this directory.
.TP
.I /home/xilinx/Vivado_Lab/2021.2/settings64.sh
Vivado Lab environment.
.TP
.IR vivado_lab*.log ", " vivado_lab*.jou
Written by Vivado into the current working directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
No variable changes the script's behaviour.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0, whatever Vivado or the reset did.
The header comment, "Usage: ./program_flash all_FPGA_AL9.sh", was copied
from another script and does not describe this one.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
/home/mu2ehwdev/boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh
/home/mu2ehwdev/boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh NORESET
/home/mu2ehwdev/boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh d
.EE
.PP
The third command is a dry run.
The
.I /home/mu2ehwdev
location of the script is the shifter convention.
In the repository the script lives in
.IR otsdaq\-mu2e/tools .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1),
.BR program_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1),
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1),
